  "narrative": "The new results strongly reinforce the accepted feature_021/outcome_006 pattern and clarify when feature_042/outcome_006 associations are not supported. I used the operational clinical anchor for outcome_006 of about 0.0175 (10% of the absolute outcome mean) and for outcome_008 of about 0.0282. The estimates are already signed to the claim direction, so a positive signed lower bound above the anchor supports the claimed clinically meaningful direction.\n\nH219-H222 directly test feature_021=1 versus feature_021=0 in feature_043-defined contexts. H219 (high feature_043) gives +0.4770, lower +0.3787; H220 (low feature_043) gives +0.3150, lower +0.2128. The extreme quartile analyses are also robust: H221 gives +0.5445, lower +0.4141, and H222 gives +0.3148, lower +0.1726. All lower bounds exceed the outcome_006 anchor by a wide margin, even with substantial multiplicity from the many overlapping subgroup tests. These claims can be accepted and closed as within-dataset evidence that the feature_021 association is not confined to one narrow feature_043 context, although the feature_043 interaction itself remains a separate conditional claim. H215 can also be closed now: its borderline interaction lower bound (+0.0206) is now supported by much stronger direct stratum-specific feature_021 contrasts, making additional investigation of that interaction unnecessary for the final dataset report.\n\nH223-H224 test feature_021/outcome_006 across observed feature_061 age strata. H223 gives +0.3543, lower +0.2447; H224 gives +0.4619, lower +0.3437. Both clear the anchor and are accepted and closed for the observed feature_061 population. Caveat: feature_061 is missing for a substantial fraction of the dataset, so these are context-specific associations among cells with observed feature_061, not general age-stratified effects.\n\nH225 and H226 test feature_042/outcome_006 among feature_021=0 individuals within high and low feature_043. Both are small and centered near zero or in the wrong direction relative to the negative-direction claims: H225 +0.0116 (lower -0.0198), H226 +0.0013 (lower -0.0280). Neither supports a clinically meaningful feature_042 association among feature_021=0 noncarriers, consistent with earlier rejection of the broader noncarrier null. These are rejected and closed.\n\nH228 tests feature_042/outcome_006 among feature_021=1 carriers in low feature_043. Its signed estimate is +0.3276 with lower +0.0819, comfortably above the anchor despite small cell sizes, so I accept it and close the direct low-feature_043 carrier claim. This supports the interpretation that the feature_042 effect is concentrated in the feature_021=1 context, especially in the low-feature_043 stratum.\n\nH227 tests the same carrier contrast in high feature_043. The point estimate is in the claimed direction (+0.1346), but the interval is wide (-0.1204 to +0.3895), crosses null, and the lower bound is far below the anchor. With only 43 exposed cells, this is underpowered and cannot distinguish attenuation in high feature_043 from a true smaller but still meaningful effect. I leave it unresolved and deferred rather than accepting or rejecting a context-specific carrier effect.\n\nH231 and H232 refine the unresolved outcome_008/feature_042 lead within feature_045=1 by feature_043. H231 gives +0.0418 with lower -0.0182; H232 gives +0.0642 with lower +0.0005. The point estimates exceed the outcome_008 anchor, but neither lower bound clears the anchor, and H232 barely clears null. Thus they do not establish a clinically anchored outcome_008 association in either feature_043 stratum. Given small cells, post-hoc splitting, and exhausted validation capacity, I defer rather than keep active strong leads. I also defer the original H202 lead for the same reason.\n\nOverall, the strongest supported within-supplied-dataset finding remains feature_021=1 being associated with a substantially higher outcome_006 score (weaker dependency) relative to feature_021=0, robust across feature_043 and observed feature_061 strata. The feature_042/outcome_006 association should be described as conditional on feature_021 carrier status, with accepted evidence among feature_021=1 carriers and rejected evidence among feature_021=0. High-feature_043 carrier decomposition and the feature_045=1 outcome_008/feature_042 lead remain uncertain and should not be presented as supported clinically meaningful associations. All statements are unadjusted, overlapping within-dataset associations, not causal or generalizable effects.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 21 appraise results. Feature_021/outcome_006 is robust: H219-H222 and H223-H224 accepted and closed; lower bounds 0.173-0.414 vs anchor 0.0175. H215 closed because direct strata support the interaction context. Feature_042/outcome_006: noncarrier contrasts H225/H226 rejected/closed; carrier low feature_043 H228 accepted/closed; carrier high feature_043 H227 unresolved/deferred due small cells and wide interval. Outcome_008 feature_042 within feature_045=1: H231/H232 unresolved/deferred because point estimates exceed anchor but lower bounds do not; H202 deferred. H229/H230 closed as unprioritized unanalyzed outcome_015/feature_034 strata. Validation capacity exhausted, so no new independent validation requested. Remaining conclusions are supplied-dataset, unadjusted, overlapping subgroup associations."
