thesis that the feature_042 contrast is more negative within feature_021=1 than in its complement. Accepted H207 directly tests feature_042 among feature_021=1 carriers and gives +0.249, interval +0.071 to +0.426; accepted H228 tests carriers in low feature_043 and gives +0.328, interval +0.082 to +0.573; accepted H203 tests feature_042 in high feature_039 and gives +0.077, interval +0.019 to +0.135. Because these claims are signed to negative-direction hypotheses, positive signed estimates support the claimed lower, stronger-dependency direction for feature_042=1 within those contexts. In contrast, unconditional feature_042/outcome_006 is not supported after validation, H46 rejected. Feature_042 among feature_021=0 is rejected, H212, as are noncarrier feature_042 contrasts within high and low feature_043, H225 and H226. The carrier high-feature_043 decomposition remains unresolved, H227, because the point estimate is positive but the interval crosses null and has only 43 exposed cells. Thus the supported statement is that feature_042/outcome_006 evidence is concentrated in defined contexts, especially feature_021=1 and selected high-feature_039 or low-feature_043 carrier strata, not that feature_042 has a robust overall association. Accepted H215 supports feature_043-related modification of the feature_021/outcome_006 association, +0.162, interval +0.021 to +0.303, but its lower bound clears the anchor only narrowly. Direct high and low feature_043 strata support both contexts clinically, so the main feature_021 effect does not depend on choosing one feature_043 stratum. H216 rejects clinically meaningful feature_039 modification of the feature_021/outcome_006 association. Unresolved or not accepted leads include outcome_008 feature_042 within feature_045=1: H202 point estimate is above the outcome_008 anchor of about 0.028, but the lower bound does not clear the anchor, and H199, H231, and H232 do not resolve it. Outcome_015 feature_034 is also unresolved because 